# Normalize EOL for all files that Git considers text files.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Live coordination state (F-318). These three are generated and append-only, and every session and
# dispatched lane on this machine reads and writes them continuously — `state.json` holds the claims
# and the in-flight board. A merge that conflicts on them writes `<<<<<<<` markers INTO the live
# files, so `state.json` stops being valid JSON while lanes are mid-task; that happened, with 12
# markers on disk and LP running. There is nothing to reconcile either: the working-tree copy is the
# superset by construction, because every agent mutates the same file.
.agent/state.json  merge=ours
.agent/BOARD.md    merge=ours
.agent/JOURNAL.md  merge=union

# docs/FINDINGS.md is deliberately NOT here — union would interleave two agents' sections and could
# split a finding in half. That file wants a real resolution.
